1. Group members feel less personally responsible for the overall task (so statement C is false);
2. Motivation decreases because members realize their individual contributions are NOT evaluated (statement A is false because it claims they ARE evaluated on an individual basis);
3. The performance of the group is not compared with that of other groups (statement B is true);
4. There is improper coordination among members (statement D is true).
Thus, statements (B) and (D) only are correct explanations.

